       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for ibuprofen is 3,200 mg/day in a monitored inpatient setting. That is twice the limit, and the usual outpatient maximum is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't make it safe.\n\nHere are some options for a corrected order:\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day), which is a common dose for pain or inflammation.\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day).\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day), or 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the ceiling).\n\nPossibly 1600 mg was meant as the total daily dose. If so, 400 mg four times daily would match it.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you really do intend 1600 mg per dose, please tell me the clinical rationale, and I'd suggest confirming it with pharmacy first."
      }
